{"agent":"pte2-kilo","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The 240 s ceiling is only applied inside `ddflow wait`/`watch` (`_call_cap` / `watch` `cap`). The change that was supposed to stop the driver from teaching `for i in seq; sleep 8..20` loops capped near 570 s is not in this change at all (manifest is only wait, watch, `[wait]` config, and tests). An agent that still follows those recipes never enters `_bounded`: given a held file it sleeps in the shell for ~570 s per iteration, so the prompt cache still goes cold and the 11.7 min claim/heartbeat+sleep path in the intent is unchanged. [D-TE-Q3] only constrains the API cap; it does not remove that loop.","digest":"6e1331809dd35513","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait_approval.py:_call_cap","malformed":"","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait_approval.py:_call_cap"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11026,"diff_sha":"302ada2006452cccbc7c394689e94d5e2aba2ab062b70d04b462ac2f7cf878b1","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/TE-poll-cadence","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":72.8,"family":"xai","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"19d5f7193505060d","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/TE-poll-cadence.rubber_duck.grok-4.7.20261111T043152Z-3915a020.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_head":"78a8cad43a52d061a4fcce78959b8e6273589a37","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait.py":"100644 60cca460fe72bb30f18ecae7d50eb3c519086a62","ddflow/api/lifecycle/wait_approval.py":"100644 3ba5e415b80f0311bdbd114a74b99d7f89609b34","ddflow/api/watch.py":"100644 4e98d7aa9781c4064862ab03558daa76320db404","ddflow/config_sections/wait.py":"100644 de37027f26fd51f1629dbb2d55f5abe1b421efdb","tests/test_wait_cadence.py":"100644 dea5a692d1